<div align="center">

# 💡 Smart Street Light using Arduino
### *Automatic Street Lighting with LDR & PIR Motion Sensor*

</div>

---

# 🎯 Project Overview

This project demonstrates a **Smart Street Light System** using an **Arduino Uno**, an **LDR (Light Dependent Resistor)**, and a **PIR Motion Sensor**. The system automatically controls street lighting based on ambient light and motion detection.

During the day, the street light remains **OFF**. At night, the PIR sensor becomes active. When motion is detected, the LED glows at **100% brightness**. If no motion is detected for **30 seconds**, the LED automatically dims to **20% brightness** to save energy.

All important events are displayed on the **Serial Monitor** with timestamps.

---

# 🚀 Objectives

🌞 Detect day and night using an LDR.

🚶 Detect human movement using a PIR sensor.

💡 Automatically control LED brightness.

⚡ Save energy by dimming the light when no motion is detected.

🖥️ Display all events with timestamps on the Serial Monitor.

---

# 🛠️ Components Required

| Component | Quantity |
|:-----------------------------|:--------:|
| Arduino Uno | 1 |
| LDR (Photoresistor) | 1 |
| 10k Ω Resistor | 1 |
| PIR Motion Sensor (HC-SR501) | 1 |
| LED | 1 |
| 220 Ω Resistor | 1 |
| Breadboard | 1 |
| Jumper Wires | As Required |

---

# 🔌 Circuit Connections

| Component | Arduino Pin |
|:----------------------|:-----------:|
| LDR Output | **A0** |
| PIR Output | **D2** |
| LED (+) | **D9 (PWM)** |
| LED (-) | **GND** |

---

# ⚙️ Working Principle

## ☀️ Step 1 – Day Detection

The Arduino continuously reads the LDR value.

If the light intensity is **above the threshold**, the system enters **Day Mode**.

- 💡 LED remains OFF
- 🚫 PIR sensor is ignored

---

## 🌙 Step 2 – Night Detection

When the LDR value falls **below the threshold**, the system enters **Night Mode**.

The PIR sensor becomes active and starts monitoring for motion.

---

## 🚶 Step 3 – Motion Detection

When the PIR sensor detects motion:

- 💡 LED brightness is set to **100% (PWM = 255)**
- ⏱️ Motion timer is reset
- 🖥️ Event is printed on the Serial Monitor

---

## 😴 Step 4 – No Motion

If no motion is detected for **30 seconds**:

- 🔅 LED brightness reduces to **20% (PWM = 51)**
- ⚡ Energy is saved while maintaining visibility

---

## 🖥️ Step 5 – Event Logging

Every important event is displayed on the **Serial Monitor** with a timestamp in **HH:MM:SS** format.

---

# ✨ Features

- 🌞 Automatic Day/Night detection
- 🚶 PIR-based motion sensing
- 💡 Automatic LED brightness control
- 🔅 Energy-saving dim mode
- ⏱️ Timestamped Serial Monitor logs
- ⚡ PWM brightness control
- 🔄 Continuous monitoring

---

# 📟 Sample Serial Monitor Output

```text
[00:00:02] EVENT: DAYLIGHT - LED OFF
[00:00:15] EVENT: Night Mode
[00:00:20] EVENT: Motion Detected - LED FULL
[00:00:50] EVENT: No Motion - LED DIM (20%)
```

---

# 🌙 Operating Modes

| Condition | LED Status |
|:---------------------|:--------------------------|
| Daylight | OFF |
| Night (No Motion) | 20% Brightness |
| Night (Motion Detected) | 100% Brightness |

---

# 🔄 Program Flow

```text
Start
   │
   ▼
Read LDR Value
   │
   ▼
Daylight?
   │
 ┌─Yes──────────────► LED OFF
 │
 └─No
      │
      ▼
Enable PIR Sensor
      │
      ▼
Motion Detected?
      │
 ┌─Yes──────────────► LED 100%
 │
 └─No
      │
      ▼
30 Seconds Passed?
      │
 ┌─Yes──────────────► LED 20%
 │
 └─No───────────────► Continue Monitoring
```

